  "term": "acceleration forces",
  "definition": "Acceleration forces are the biomechanical forces produced when the head is rapidly sped up or its motion is changed. In this context, they refer to the head-movement forces used to model the kind of mechanical impact seen in human mild traumatic brain injury.",
